    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Gary O'Driscoll & Co. Ltd are delighted to bring to the market Leampreaghane, Kilflynn, a substantial four-bedroom detached bungalow set on a large site extending to approximately 1.45 acres. Extending to approximately 3,700 sq. ft. internally, this impressive property offers generous accommodation throughout together with excellent outdoor space.\n\nThe property comprises four spacious double bedrooms, with the master bedroom benefiting from an en-suite and walk-in wardrobe. The property also benefits from stairwell access to a large attic storage area, providing extensive additional storage space.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises entrance hallway, sitting room, hallway, kitchen/breakfast room, dining room, utility room, four double bedrooms, en-suite, walk-in wardrobe and main bathroom. The kitchen/dining area benefits from a large solid fuel stove, while heating is provided by oil-fired central heating.\n\nThe property is constructed with cavity walls and benefits from double-glazed golden oak PVC windows and a concrete tile roof. Externally, the property is further enhanced by a large block-built garage and generous grounds extending to approximately 1.45 acres. A septic tank is located to the rear of the property.\n\nAccommodation:\n\nEntrance Hallway: 5.71m x 2.10m\nSitting Room: 4.54m x 5.44m\nHallway: 14.36m x 1.27m\nKitchen/Breakfast Room: 6.07m x 9.41m\nDining Room: 5.17m x 3.43m\nUtility Room: 4.18m x 2.12m\nMaster Bedroom: 4.20m x 6.07m\nEn-Suite: 2.17m x 1.93m\nWalk-in Wardrobe: 2.17m x 1.93m\nBedroom 2: 5.44m x 4.00m\nMain Bathroom: 4.18m x 2.37m\nBedroom 3: 3.94m x 5.24m\nBedroom 4: 3.50m x 5.24m\n\nAttic / Storage Accommodation:\n\nLanding / Storage: 10.87m x 6.44m\nStore Room 1: 5.22m x 4.31m\nStore Room 2: 5.28m x 4.30m\n\nLeampreaghane offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial detached family home in a peaceful rural setting, while remaining within easy reach of the village of Kilflynn and the surrounding North Kerry area. The combination of extensive internal accommodation, four double bedrooms, generous attic storage, a large garage and a 1.45-acre site makes this a property with considerable appeal and potential."
      },
